            <ArticleTitle>A novel mutation in the JH4 domain of JAK3 causing severe combined immunodeficiency complicated by vertebral osteomyelitis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>198-200</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1521-6616(17)30663-0</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.clim.2017.09.007</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>JAK3 is a tyrosine kinase essential for signaling downstream of the common gamma chain subunit shared by multiple cytokine receptors. JAK3 deficiency results in T-B+NK- severe combined immune deficiency (SCID). We report a patient with SCID due to a novel mutation in the JAK3 JH4 domain. The function of the JH4 domain remains unknown. This is the first report of a missense mutation in the JAK3 JH4 domain, thereby demonstrating the importance of the JH4 domain of JAK3 in host immunity.</AbstractText>
